# Root .dockerignore — applies to any `docker build` that uses the repo root
# as its build context, which is how the self-host stack builds its api/web
# images.
#
# Without this, `COPY workers/api/ ./workers/api/` (or any future Dockerfile
# doing the same) would pull real local secrets into the build-stage image
# layer — retrievable later via `docker history` / BuildKit cache / a
# `--target` save of that stage even though the final runtime stage never
# copies them forward. Mirrors this repo's own .gitignore secret patterns.

# Local secrets — never let any image build stage see these.
#
# NOTE: unlike .gitignore, Docker's .dockerignore does NOT match a bare
# filename pattern (e.g. `.dev.vars`) at any depth — it only matches at the
# context root (per Docker's documented filepath.Match-based semantics).
# Every pattern below is listed both bare (root-level files like the repo's
# own .env.key/.env.resend) and `**/`-prefixed (nested files like
# workers/api/.dev.vars, apps/web/.env.local) — verified by direct build
# reproduction, not assumed.
.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
**/.dev.vars.*
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Build artifacts / dependency trees — regenerated inside the build stage,
# never needed (and often stale/host-specific) from the host filesystem.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.wrangler/
**/.wrangler/
